## ...........................................................................
## DNA nucleotides, added for the nucleosome demo (not part of gcf_rje23_v14)
##
## pdb2pimms gives DNA nucleotides the bead types a, c, g and t. Each nucleotide
## carries one phosphate, so each is modelled as a single negative charge: it
## takes the aspartate (D) charge terms with K, R, D and E (short, long and
## super-long range), the D-D terms with every nucleotide, the D solvation
## energy, and no interaction with any other bead. The DNA is frozen in the
## demo, so its angle penalties never change; they are zero.
## ...........................................................................

ANGLE_PENALTY	a	0	0	0
ANGLE_PENALTY	c	0	0	0
ANGLE_PENALTY	g	0	0	0
ANGLE_PENALTY	t	0	0	0

a	0	-4
c	0	-4
g	0	-4
t	0	-4

